        "question":  "You are called to evaluate a potentially delirious patient on a medical unit. As part of your workup you order an EEG. What do you expect to find on EEG if this is truly a delirium?",
        "choices":  [
                        "3-per-second spike and wave pattern",
                        "Frontocentral beta activity",
                        "Posterior alpha rhythm",
                        "Generalized slow-wave activity consisting of theta and delta waves, as well as some focal areas of hyperactivity",
                        "Right temporal spikes"
                    ],
