        "explanation":  "Whereas some MAOIs work on both MAO-A and MAO-B, selegiline works selectively on MAO-B at lower doses. MAO-A is involved in the metabolism of serotonin and norepinephrine. MAO-B is involved in the metabolism of phenylethylamine. Both are involved in the metabolism of dopamine. MAO-A in the gastrointestinal tract is involved in the metabolism of tyramine. If you block these enzymes, tyramine is not broken down, which can lead to hypertensive crisis. Psychopharmacology K\u0026S Chapter 29",
