        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The prefrontal cortices influence mood differently. If one activates the left prefrontal cortex, mood is lifted. If the right prefrontal cortex is activated, mood is depressed. Therefore a lesion to the left prefrontal cortex would cause depression, and a lesion to the right prefrontal cortex would cause euphoria and laughter. The parietal and occipital lobes are not the predominant lobes involved in emotion. Basic Neuroscience K\u0026S Chapter 1",
