        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The raphe nuclei of the brainstem, predominantly in the pons, are the major sites of serotonergic cell bodies. The ventral tegmental area, substantia nigra, and nucleus accumbens are all dopaminergic areas and are parts of the major neuronal pathways involved in the pathophysiology of schizophrenia. The cerebellum is a distractor. Basic Neuroscience K\u0026S Chapter 1",
