        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Aaron Beck is the originator of cognitive behavioral therapy. In this theory, patients\u0027 assumptions affect their cognitions, which in turn affect their mood. As such, it would be cognitive distortion that Beck would most likely find as the cause of depression. The other answer choices may be things to which other theorists attribute depression or are totally unrelated answer choices included to distract. Psychotherapy K\u0026S Chapter 28",
        "image":  null
