        "explanation":  "APP is the protein that makes up the amyloid plaques found in the brain in Alzheimer\u0027s disease. The protein is encoded by a gene found on chromosome 21. The amyloid deposits found in Alzheimer\u0027s disease are the hallmark of the disease\u0027s neuropathology. Wilson\u0027s disease is the result of abnormal copper metabolism, not amyloid. Schizophrenia, bipolar disorder, and HD have nothing to do with amyloid. Neurocognitive Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 10",
