        "question":  "While on call in the emergency room, you receive a phone call from emergency medical services (EMS) to say that they are bringing in a patient who is highly intoxicated and behaviorally out of control. The patient\u0027s friend told EMS that the patient has been taking amphetamines. If this is true, what is the most prominent psychiatric symptom you would expect to see?",
