        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "Beneficence",
        "explanation":  "Beneficence is the duty to do no harm to the patient. Autonomy is the duty to protect a patient\u0027s freedom to choose. Autonomy theory views the relationship between patient and doctor as between two adults, not as parent and child. Justice in this context means a fair distribution and application of services. Validity is a statistical word meaning that a test measures what it claims to measure. Ethics K\u0026S Chapter 36",
