        "question":  "A 45-year-old woman presents to your office complaining of long-standing lower extremity discomfort, particularly at night before sleep onset. She reports shooting pains in the lower extremities that are relieved upon standing or walking. The discomfort is described as a \"crawling\" sensation. The treatment of choice for her condition is:",
