        "explanation":  "The most common hallucinations in schizophrenia are auditory. Visual, olfactory, and tactile hallucinations are also possible. Schizophrenia was first discovered by Morel, who called it \"d-mence precoce.\" Later Kraepelin used \"dementia praecox\" to describe a group of illnesses that started in adolescence and ended in dementia. Bleuler coined the term \"schizophrenia.\" The disorder is chronic and has a prodromal, active, and residual phase. Psychotic Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 7",
