        "answerText":  "Intramuscular phenytoin",
        "explanation":  "Intramuscular phenytoin is a poor choice for treatment of status epilepticus because of its erratic rate of absorption. Useful status epilepticus treatments include rectal or intravenous diazepam, intravenous lorazepam, intravenous phenytoin or fosphenytoin, intravenous valproic acid, oxygen by nasal cannula and airway protection, and intravenous phenobarbital. Phenobarbital is acceptable treatment but not the best choice because of the narrow therapeutic window and possibility of overdose leading to respiratory depression and possible death. Neurology B\u0026D Chapter 67",
