        "explanation":  "The condition noted in this question is that of the classic Brown-S-quard syndrome due to a hemisection of the spinal cord. The correct combination of deficits is that of loss of motor control and posterior column function ipsilateral to and below the level of the lesion coupled with contralateral loss of pain and temperature sensation one to two dermatomal levels below the level of the lesion. Frequent causes include disk herniation, penetrating trauma, spinal fracture, and radiation injury. The cervical spinal cord is most commonly affected. Neurology B\u0026D Chapter 24",
