        "explanation":  "The six biogenic amine neurotransmitters are dopamine, epinephrine, NE, acetylcholine, histamine, and serotonin. Of these, dopamine, NE, and epinephrine are all synthesized from the precursor tyrosine and are known as a group as the catecholamines. GABA is an amino acid neurotransmitter, not a biogenic amine. Of note is that cocaine works by blocking the reuptake of the biogenic amines, more specifically serotonin, NE, and dopamine. Basic Neuroscience K\u0026S Chapter 1",
