        "explanation":  "To diagnose schizophrenia, active-phase symptoms must be present for a 1-month period only. It may be diagnosed if other symptoms (i.e., negative) are present over a 6-month period, but active-phase symptoms must be present for at least 1 month of those 6 months. All other answer choices are part of the characteristic active-phase symptoms for schizophrenia. Social isolation is a bad prognostic sign for schizophrenia. Good prognostic signs include late age of onset, acute onset, and the presence of an affective component. Psychotic Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 7",
