        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "A cohort study is when a group from a well-known population is chosen and followed over a long period of time. These studies give us estimates of risk based on suspected causative factors for a given disease. Case history studies look back on people with a given disease. Cross-sectional studies give information on the prevalence of a disease in a population at a given point in time. Retrospective studies are based on past data, as opposed to prospective studies, which are based on observing things as they occur. Statistics K\u0026S Chapter 5",
