        "explanation":  "Fiduciary duty is the obligation to work in the patient\u0027s best interests. Beneficence is an obligation to help patients and relieve suffering. Nonmaleficence is the duty to do no harm. Altruism is putting the needs of others before your own needs. Parens patriae is a doctrine that allows the state to intervene and act as a surrogate parent for those who cannot take care of themselves. Ethics K\u0026S Chapter 36",
