        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The practice described in the question is called \"fee splitting\" and is considered unethical. As a physician you cannot receive financial compensation for referring patients to other doctors, nor can you pay for such referrals. Such an arrangement puts the doctor\u0027s interests (the financial incentive to refer) over the best interests of the patient and leads to inappropriate referrals. Ethics K\u0026S Chapter 36",
