        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The MCA territory includes the optic radiations. A lesion of these tracts results in either a contralateral homonymous hemianopsia or a contralateral inferior quadrantanopia (\"pie on the floor\"). Bitemporal hemianopsia is of course caused by invasion of the optic chiasm, often by a sellar lesion, such as a pituitary macroadenoma. Left monocular blindness would result from an ipsilateral central retinal artery occlusion. Neurology B\u0026D Chapter 51",
        "image":  null
