        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Secondary gain refers to tangible advantages that a patient may get as a result of being unwell. Examples of secondary gain include getting out of responsibility; getting money, drugs, or other financial entitlements; or controlling other people\u0027s behavior. Getting or seeking medical help, or enjoying playing the sick role for its own sake, would be considered a form of primary gain. Somatic Symptom Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 13",
