        "explanation":  "In hypothyroidism, one would expect to find an increased TSH and a low free T4 level. Subclinical cases of hypothyroidism will present with a high TSH and a normal T4 level. Other answer choices are distractors and are not the most important laboratory values to look for when trying to diagnose hypothyroidism. Laboratory Tests in Psychiatry K\u0026S Chapter 5",
