        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "OCD is believed to be a result of an imbalance in the serotonin system. Data show that serotonergic drugs are more effective in relieving symptoms of OCD than drugs that work on other neurotransmitter systems. Studies are unclear as to whether serotonin actually is involved in the cause of OCD. CSF assays of 5-HIAA have reported variable findings in patients with OCD. In one study, CSF levels of 5-HIAA decreased after treatment with clomipramine, leading researchers to the conclusion that the serotonin system is involved in OCD symptom genesis. Obsessive Compulsive and Related Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 10",
