        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "This question focuses on Piaget\u0027s stages of cognitive development. (Just in case you don\u0027t have it mastered after Test Two.) In the concrete operations stage, egocentric thought changes to operational thought in which another\u0027s point of view can be taken into consideration. In concrete operations, children can put things in order and group objects according to common characteristics. They develop the understanding of conservation (a tall cup and a wide cup can both hold equal volumes of water) and reversibility (ice can change to water and back to ice again). Human Development K\u0026S Chapter 2",
