        "question":  "A middle-aged man has been referred to your office by a plastic surgeon. The man is seeking a face lift for his \"excessively large cheeks.\" The surgeon has not been able to find anything abnormal about the man\u0027s face or skin, and when he comes to see you, you fail to see anything wrong either. The patient insists that his cheeks are grotesque and ruining his whole appearance. When pressed, he admits that others may not consider his cheeks to be as bad as he does. His most likely diagnosis is:",
