        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The primary auditory cortex localizes to the superior temporal gyrus (Heschl\u0027s gyrus) in both temporal lobes. Cortical deafness can result from bilateral strokes to the temporal lobes that destroy Heschl\u0027s gyri. The thalamus is of course the relay station for much of the sensory input to the brain. The frontal lobes are responsible for attention, concentration, set-shifting, organization and executive functioning, and planning. The occipital lobes are the location of the calcarine cortex, which is responsible for interpreting and processing visual input and stimuli. Neurology B\u0026D Chapters 11 and 12",
