        "explanation":  "Gabapentin and pregabalin are both U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA)-approved for the systemic oral treatment of postherpetic neuralgia. The lidocaine transdermal patch (Lidoderm) is FDA-approved for the topical and local treatment of postherpetic neuralgic pain. Carbamazepine and oxcarbazepine are not FDA-approved, but both have been shown to be acceptable alternatives for the treatment of trigeminal and postherpetic neuralgia. Phenytoin, an anticonvulsant agent, has no place in the treatment of postherpetic neuralgia. Neurology B\u0026D Chapters 44 and 67",
