        "vignetteStem":  "",
        "question":  "A construction worker was standing very near a three-story scaffold that fell and missed crushing him by inches. Four days later he reports feeling anxiety; a sense of numbing, detachment, and difficulty remembering the accident; and he states that he feels like he\u0027s in a daze. The most likely diagnosis is:",
