        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Although one could argue for bits and pieces of other diagnoses, when taking the whole picture into consideration, this patient is a case of borderline personality disorder. Borderline personality disorder is characterized by frantic efforts to avoid abandonment, unstable interpersonal relationships, disturbed self-image, impulsive behavior, recurrent suicidality or self-mutilation, affective instability, chronic feelings of emptiness, intense anger, and stress-related paranoia or severe dissociative symptoms. The woman in the question clearly presents with many of these symptoms. Personality Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 22",
