        "vignetteStem":  "",
        "question":  "A 59-year-old man comes into your office complaining of depression. His wife of 25 years died unexpectedly 5 weeks before. Since then he has been crying, has had little appetite but has lost no weight, and reports difficulty sleeping. He has been going out to dinner once each week with friends and says that it helps get his mind off of his wife\u0027s death. He is not suicidal. This is the first time in his life that he has had symptoms such as these. His most likely diagnosis is:",
