        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "All of this question\u0027s answer choices are criteria for diagnosis of kleptomania, except that, before the theft, the patient has an increased sense of tension. Kleptomania is found within the larger heading of impulse control disorders. In kleptomania the patient engages in repeated stealing of objects that he or she does not need. An important part of the disorder is the sense of tension before the act and the sense of pleasure or relief afterward. Disruptive, Impulse Control, Conduct Disorders, and ADHD K\u0026S Chapter 19",
