        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "This is a case of intermittent explosive disorder. The patient has a history of violent outbursts that are out of proportion to the severity of the situation in which they occur. He has no other signs or symptoms that would suggest another Axis I or II diagnosis. He has no medical history that would suggest that he could have a seizure disorder or that would otherwise explain his behavior. Disruptive, Impulse Control, Conduct Disorders, and ADHD K\u0026S Chapter 19",
