        "explanation":  "The caudate nucleus neurons have many D2 receptors. They regulate motor activity by determining which motor acts get carried out. With blockade of the caudate D2 receptors, bradykinesia develops from excessive dampening of motor activity. With caudate D2 receptor overstimulation, tics and extraneous motor movements develop. This is important to understanding the role of the caudate in Parkinson\u0027s, Tourette\u0027s and tics. Basic Neuroscience K\u0026S Chapter 1",
