        "answerText":  "Euphoria",
        "explanation":  "Euphoria is a behavioral effect of opioids, as are drowsiness, decreased sex drive, hypoactivity, and personality changes. Miosis is a physical effect of opioid use. Increased arousal is not an effect of opioid intoxication, drowsiness is. Diarrhea can come from withdrawal, but opioids themselves cause constipation. Bradycardia is also a physical effect of opioids, and as such tachycardia is incorrect. Substance Abuse and Addictive Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 20",
