        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The therapeutic range for lithium is 0.6 to 1.2 mEq/L. Toxic levels are 2 mEq/L or higher. Lethal levels are 4.0 mEq/L or higher. Bonus Fact: For a patient who needs regular dialysis and for whom lithium is the best medication...give a dose of lithium immediately after the dialysis. Laboratory Tests in Psychiatry K\u0026S Chapter 29",
