        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Common side effects of valproic acid include weight gain, tremor, thinning of the hair, and ankle swelling. Other noted adverse effects are gastrointestinal distress, sedation, pancreatitis, bone marrow suppression (pancytopenia), and hepatotoxicity. The agent is teratogenic, and the most worrisome fetotoxic effect is the neural tube defect (spina bifida), which is dangerous during neurogenesis in the first trimester of gestation. Psychopharmacology B\u0026D Chapter 67",
