        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The relative risk of an illness is the ratio of the incidence of the condition in those with risk factors to the incidence of the condition in those without risk factors. Attributable risk refers to the absolute incidence of the illness in patients exposed to the condition that can be attributed to the exposure. The other answer choices are nonsense distractors and are not true biostatistical terms. Statistics K\u0026S Chapter 5",
