        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Patients being started on clozapine should have a baseline WBC count with differential before treatment. A WBC count with differential is taken every week during treatment for the first 6 months, then every 2 weeks thereafter. Monthly monitoring of WBC count may be done after 12 months of therapy on clozapine. When treatment is stopped, WBC counts should be taken every week for 4 weeks. It is not a part of standard monitoring to take two WBC counts in 1 week. Laboratory Tests in Psychiatry K\u0026S Chapter 29",
