        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "To meet criteria for the rapid cycling specifier in bipolar disorder, the patient must present with at least four mood episodes over the past 12 months. The mood episodes must meet criteria for a major depressive, manic, mixed, or hypomanic episode. Female patients are more likely than men to have rapid cycling bipolar disorder. There is no evidence to suggest that rapid cycling is a heritable phenomenon in bipolar disorder. It is therefore likely to be a result of external factors, such as stress or medication. Bipolar Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 8",
