        "question":  "A psychiatrist interviews a Japanese immigrant who was brought to the hospital by her family for depression. In the meeting with her she does not endorse any significant symptoms. When speaking to the family, they state that she has been having many of the symptoms that she previously denied. Which one of the following is the most likely explanation for this situation?",
