        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Anton\u0027s syndrome is considered to be an agnosia characterized by cortical blindness. The lesion localizes to the bilateral occipital lobes, usually due to strokes, particularly in the calcarine cortex (Brodmann\u0027s area 17) and visual association cortex. The hallmark of the syndrome is that patients deny that they are blind and they confabulate. Patients may also suffer from visual hallucinations. Neurology B\u0026D Chapter 14",
