        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Riluzole (Rilutek) is a glutamate antagonist and is FDA-approved in the treatment of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS). It has demonstrated mild-to-moderate improvement in the survival rate of ALS. It may also help patients remain in a milder disease state for a longer period of time. Side effects include gastrointestinal upset, dizziness, fatigue, and liver enzyme elevation. The other answer choices are distractors. Neurology B\u0026D Chapter 74",
