        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Pancreatic cancer has been associated with a high rate of depression. Patients present with apathy, decreased energy, and anhedonia. It should be a consideration in the clinician\u0027s mind whenever seeing middle-aged depressed patients. Cancer in general brings about many psychological reactions in patients. Fear of death, fear of abandonment and disfigurement, loss of independence, denial, anxiety, guilt, financial worries, and disruption in relationships all play a role. Of patients with cancer, 50% often have comorbid psychiatric diagnoses, with adjustment disorder, major depressive disorder, and delirium being the most common. Depressive Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 13",
