        "explanation":  "It is the GABA-A receptor that has binding sites for the benzodiazepines. There are three types of GABA receptors, GABA-A, -B, and -C. There are no GABA-D or GABA-E receptors. The benzodiazepines increase the affinity of the GABA-A receptor for GABA. The GABA-A receptor is a chloride ion channel. Psychopharmacology K\u0026S Chapter 1",
