        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The TCAs venlafaxine, bupropion, and nefazodone block the reuptake of NE (and serotonin in some cases) into the presynaptic neuron. This leads to more NE in the synaptic cleft. Mirtazapine works by blocking presynaptic 2 receptors, which stops feedback inhibition on the release of NE into the synaptic cleft. This results in more NE released into the synapse. Psychopharmacology K\u0026S Chapter 29",
        "image":  null
