        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The three best benzodiazepines for patients with liver dysfunction are temazepam, oxazepam, and lorazepam. This is an important little fact for the well-prepared test-taker to know. They have short half-lives and do not have active metabolites. Other benzodiazepines are less desirable in patients with hepatic dysfunction. Psychopharmacology K\u0026S Chapter 29",
