        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Mirtazapine is an antidepressant medication that works by antagonism of presynaptic 2 adrenergic receptors leading to potentiation of serotonergic and noradrenergic neurotransmission. Mirtazapine is sedating, particularly at low doses, which is good for depressed patients with insomnia. It lacks the anticholinergic side effects of the tricyclics and lacks the anxiogenic side effects of the serotonin-selective reuptake inhibitors. Mirtazapine is also notable for its lack of sexual side effects. Other psychiatric medications notable for their lack of sexual side effects include bupropion, buspirone, donepezil, galantamine, and nefazodone. Psychopharmacology K\u0026S Chapter 29",
