        "explanation":  "Intracranial metastatic carcinoma is more frequently seen than primary brain tumors. Most carcinomas metastasize to the brain via hematogenous spread. About one-third of brain metastases originate in the lung, and about half that number originate in the breast. The third most frequent source is melanoma, followed by the GI tract, in particular the colon and the rectum. This is followed in frequency by cancers of the kidney. The remainder are accounted for by cancers of the thyroid, liver, gallbladder, testicle, pancreas, uterus, and ovaries. Neurology B\u0026D Chapter 52F",
