        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "For the individual to be rendered unconscious by a traumatic brain lesion, either the reticular activating system or diffuse injury to both hemispheres must be involved. The functioning of the awake mind requires the ascending inputs referred to as the reticular activating system, with its way stations in the brain stem and thalamus, as well as an intact cerebral cortex. Bilateral lesions of the brain stem or the thalamus produce coma. Very diffuse lesions of the hemispheres produce an \"awake\" patient who shows no responsiveness to the environment in a persistent vegetative state. Patients with very slight responses to environmental stimuli are said to be in a minimally conscious state. Neurology B\u0026D Chapter 6",
