        "question":  "Transcranial magnetic stimulation was cleared by the FDA in 2008 for in-office treatment of major depressive disorder. The area of the brain that is treated with electromagnetic stimulus application is first mapped by finding the motor threshold at the area on the motor strip corresponding to the thumb and fingers. After the discovery of the best area of motor threshold by this mapping, the ongoing treatment is applied to approximately which of the following brain areas?",
