        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "When lamotrigine and valproic acid are given together, lamotrigine levels are elevated, and valproic acid levels are decreased. When lamotrigine and carbamazepine are given together, lamotrigine levels are decreased. Valproic acid will increase carbamazepine levels. Because lithium is cleared renally, it will not affect the levels of lamotrigine, valproic acid, or carbamazepine. Psychopharmacology K\u0026S Chapter 29",
