        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Lithium is cleared through the kidneys. It is reabsorbed in the proximal tubules with sodium. When a thiazide diuretic, such as hydrochlorothiazide, is added, it leads to sodium depletion, which in turn causes the reabsorption of sodium and lithium in the proximal tubules. This increased lithium reabsorption added to the lower fluid levels as a result of the diuretic can lead to an increased lithium level and lithium toxicity. Valproic acid and clozapine are metabolized through the liver and would not be affected by a thiazide diuretic. Psychopharmacology K\u0026S Chapter 29",
        "image":  null
