        "vignetteStem":  "",
        "question":  "A 70-year-old woman complains of leg stiffness while ambulating and lower extremity spasms while trying to sleep. Neurologic examination reveals a markedly stiff-legged gait, with leg adduction while walking. Lower extremity tone is increased with a spastic catch. Knee-jerk reflexes are hyperactive, and ankle-jerk reflexes elicit clonus. Romberg testing reveals sway when the patient closes her eyes. The most likely diagnosis in this case is:",
