        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Encopresis is defined by DSM 5 as the repeated passage of feces into inappropriate places, such as clothes or the floor, whether intentionally or involuntarily. The child must be 4 years of age or older. The episodes must occur at least monthly for 3 months or more. Encopresis is not due to a general medical condition. The behavior must cause the child significant distress or social or academic impairment. Boys are found to have encopresis six times more frequently than girls. Encopresis has been shown to develop with much greater frequency in children with a known history of sexual abuse. Some studies have associated encopresis with measures of maternal hostility and punitive and harsh parenting. Elimination Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 31",
