        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "In binge eating disorder, there are recurrent episodes of binge eating consisting of eating rapidly, eating until uncomfortably full, eating large amounts of food when not hungry, eating alone because of embarrassment about eating, or feeling disgusted with oneself, depressed, or guilty after eating. It is differentiated from bulimia nervosa by a lack of inappropriate compensatory behaviors, such as vomiting, laxative use, or excessive exercise. Feeding and Eating Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 15",
