        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The addition of a benzodiazepine to a patient on an SSRI for panic disorder will lead to a more rapid resolution of the anxiety. The SSRI will take 2 to 4 weeks to work in most cases. The benzodiazepine can effectively control the patient\u0027s symptoms until the SSRI is fully working. The other choices will take longer to titrate or become effective and are not good choices for rapid resolution of panic symptoms. Propranolol is indicated only for performance anxiety and should not be used in other anxiety disorders. Anxiety Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 9",
