        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Lithium has been associated with hyperplasia and adenomas of the parathyroid glands leading to hyperparathyroidism and hypercalcemia. Neutropenia is associated with clozapine. Pancreatitis is a rare but potentially deadly side effect of valproic acid. Hepatic failure is associated with valproic acid, hence the black box warning in the Physician\u0027s Desk Reference. Eosinophilic colitis is associated with clozapine. Though these drugs are certainly not the only causes of these conditions, these associations would be useful for the prudent student to know. Psychopharmacology K\u0026S Chapter 29",
        "image":  null
