        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "DSM 5 criteria for panic disorder state that the patient must have recurrent attacks of which at least one is followed by 1 month or more of persistent concern about having more attacks, worry about the implications of the attack or its consequences, or a significant change in behavior related to the attacks. Anxiety Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 9",
