        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "The DSM 5 states that to meet criteria for generalized anxiety disorder, excessive anxiety and worry about a number of events or activities must occur more days than not for at least 6 months. The individual finds it difficult to control the worry. The worry is associated with symptoms such as restlessness, fatigue, difficulty concentrating, irritability, muscle tension, or sleep disturbance. It causes impairment in social or occupational functioning. It is not attributable to substance abuse or another mental disorder. Lifetime prevalence of generalized anxiety disorder is around 5%. Anxiety Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 9",
