        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Symptoms of pheochromocytoma can include anxiety, panic, tremulousness, flushing, feeling of impending doom, hypertension, and tachycardia. It can be mistaken for panic disorder. Hyperparathyroidism presents as constipation, polydipsia, nausea, depression, paranoia, and confusion. Hypothyroidism presents with cold intolerance, weight gain, brittle hair, goiter, constipation, dry skin, lethargy, depressed affect, hallucinations, and paranoia. Raynaud\u0027s phenomenon presents with idiopathic paroxysmal bilateral cyanosis of the digits and can be exacerbated or triggered by stress. Crohn\u0027s disease does not have psychiatric manifestations. Somatic Symptom Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 13",
