        "isMultiSelect":  false,
        "answerText":  "",
        "explanation":  "Regularly scheduled primary care appointments are a crucial and standard part of treating illness anxiety disorder. In illness anxiety disorder the patients are convinced that they have an illness that they don\u0027t have. If they are not followed closely by their primary care physician, they will go doctor shopping. While regularly following up with the primary care doctor, they should also be engaged in psychotherapy to work on the underlying psychological causes of the condition. None of the other disorders listed require regular follow-up by the primary care doctor. That is not to say these patients should not regularly follow-up for routine medical care, but that it is not a crucial component of the treatment for the psychiatric condition. Somatic Symptom Disorders K\u0026S Chapter 13",
