        "explanation":  "A workup for Carl should include thyroid function tests, as thyroid disorders can mimic mood disorders and must be ruled out. Nocturnal polysomnography (sleep study) is the test of choice to diagnose sleep apnea. A periodic limb movements of sleep test is not a real test. There is a periodic limb movements of sleep disorder (restless legs syndrome). It is diagnosed with nocturnal polysomnography, but there is not a special test with that name. CPAP is the machine used to treat sleep apnea. It does not diagnose sleep apnea. Therefore it would not be used as part of a workup. K\u0026S Chapter 16",
