        "explanation":  "Affect is the patient\u0027s present emotional responsiveness based on facial expressions and expressive behavior. It may or may not be congruent with mood. Words used to describe affect include full range (within normal range), constricted, blunted, and flat. Full range would be considered normal. Flat would be used to describe a patient who is showing no signs of affective expression. A patient with constricted affect shows less emotion than someone who is full range but more than someone who is blunted. Someone who is blunted shows less emotion than someone who is constricted but more than someone who is flat. K\u0026S Chapter 5",
